&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9,824&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2027&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9,331&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2028&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9,389&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2029&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9,365&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2030&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9,236&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2031-2035&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;42,603&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Postretirement Benefit Plan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company sponsors a postretirement benefit plan which provides life insurance benefits to retirees. This plan is unfunded and the projected benefit obligation was $12.9&#160;million and $12.8&#160;million at December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAccountingForTheRespondentSPensionsAndPostretirementBenefitsTextBlock>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-22" contextRef="c-1">2026-06-09</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfDetailsOnAccountingForIncomeTaxesTextBlock id="f-23" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:8pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Consistent with prior years, income tax-related balances reflected within Colonial&#8217;s balance sheet and income statement were prepared in accordance with the U.S. Internal Revenue Code and support the Company&#8217;s federal, state, and other jurisdictional income tax return filing processes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:8pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Information concerning the Company&#8217;s deferred taxes is included on the Analysis of Federal Income and Other Taxes Deferred schedule that is located at Page 230 within this Form 6 report. The change in the Company&#8217;s unrecognized tax benefits during the year were immaterial.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:8pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company files income tax returns with the IRS and states in which Colonial operates or has employees. As of December 31, 2025, the Company's tax years 2022 through 2024 are subject to examination by the IRS and the Company's tax years 2021 through 2024 are subject to examination by certain state and local authorities. Colonial is not currently under examination by either the IRS or state or local authorities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfDetailsOnAccountingForIncomeTaxesTextBlock>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-24" contextRef="c-1">2026-06-09</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantRateOrOtherRegulatoryMattersTextBlock id="f-25" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Matters Pertaining to Customer Actions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:5pt;padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On November 22, 2017, three of Colonial's shippers filed a complaint with the FERC challenging the Company's rates as unjust and unreasonable. Several other Colonial Pipeline shippers filed similar complaints or motions to intervene. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On September 20, 2018, the FERC issued an order to consolidate the complaints. As part of the order, the FERC established separate proceedings for complaints regarding (a) Colonial Pipeline's market-based rates and (b) Colonial Pipeline's index-based rates and product loss recovery practices. The hearings commenced in September 2020 and concluded in December&#160;2020. On December 1, 2021, the presiding judge issued a non-binding partial initial decision pertaining to Colonial's market-based rates and product loss recovery practices. The judge recommended that Colonial retain its market-based rate authority, with one exception. On April&#160;27, 2022, the presiding judge issued a non-binding second partial initial decision related to Colonial's index rates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On November 16, 2023, the FERC ruled on the exceptions to both Initial Decisions. In the FERC's market-based rates and product loss recovery practices order (Order No. 585), the Commission upheld Colonial's market-based rate authority in all challenged markets and found that reparations are not owed for the matters addressed within Order No. 585. The Commission ruled on several index-based rates issues in Order No. 586. Order No. 586 affirmed several Colonial positions while also ruling against the Company on certain positions and did not opine on whether Colonial's index rates were unjust and unreasonable. The Company submitted compliance filings in January&#160;2024 for both orders and filed a tariff for its product loss recovery practices. On March 26, 2024, the FERC issued an order accepting and suspending the tariff, effective April&#160;1, 2024, subject to refund. Colonial subsequently made additional product loss recovery-related filings, which the FERC accepted effective April&#160;1,&#160;2025. During the first eight months of 2024, Colonial settled with several shippers who subsequently submitted Notices of Withdrawal from the challenge to the Company's rates. On August 30, 2024, Colonial submitted a settlement agreement involving all remaining parties. On October 31, 2024, FERC approved the settlement agreement, and Colonial's prospective index rates applicable to all shippers became effective November 1, 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On February 1, 2024, one of Colonial's shippers filed a new complaint with the FERC asserting that the Company's indexed rates are unjust and unreasonable and further challenging the Company's market-based rates. Five additional shippers subsequently filed similar complaints. On April 2, 2025, the FERC issued an order consolidating the six complaints that were outstanding as of that date into one proceeding (Docket No. OR24-3). With that order, the FERC also dismissed the challenges to Colonial's market-based rates and referred the challenges to the indexed rates to a hearing process, suspending that hearing process pending a FERC settlement process. On May 23, 2025, a seventh shipper filed a complaint (Docket No. OR25-8). On September&#160;24, 2025, this shipper's complaint was consolidated into the same proceeding as the previously filed six complaints. As of the date of this report, Colonial has settled with four of the seven shippers. Colonial has substantial defenses to the remaining complaints and will vigorously assert these defenses. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;FERC Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The FERC indexing system provides for annual index rate adjustments effective no earlier than July 1st of each year. The indexing system currently applies to a majority of the Company&#8217;s published tariff rates. Colonial elected to adjust its index rates in each of the years presented within this report in keeping with the FERC indexing system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On November 20, 2025, the FERC issued a Notice of Proposed Rulemaking (NOPR) to seek comment on a proposed index level used to determine annual changes to oil pipeline rate ceilings for the five-year period commencing on July 1, 2026. The FERC has proposed to use the Producer Price Index for Finished Goods (PPI-FG) minus 1.42% as the index level for the five-year period commencing July 1, 2026. Comments to this NOPR have been submitted.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Tax-Free Reorganization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Effective February 1, 2025, Colonial completed a tax-free reorganization under Sections 368 and 355 of the Internal Revenue Code (tax-free spin) whereby Colonial's entire equity interests in two wholly-owned, non-jurisdictional subsidiaries that are not engaged in transportation services were distributed to its parent company, Colonial Enterprises, Inc. Colonial recorded a net distribution of $196.3 million against Account 75 - Unappropriated Retained Income within the Comparative Balance Sheet Statement to reflect this transaction. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Subsequent Events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Colonial has evaluated events subsequent to the balance sheet date but prior to June&#160;9, 2026, the date the financial statements were available for issuance, that would have a material impact on these Form 6 financial statements. Any material subsequent events that occurred during this time have been properly disclosed in the accompanying notes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantRateOrOtherRegulatoryMattersTextBlock>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-26" contextRef="c-1">2026-06-09</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:ReportDate id="f-27" contextRef="c-1">2026-06-09</ferc:ReportDate>
  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-28" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4. See Notes to Financial Statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-29" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements are presented in accordance with U.S. generally accepted accounting principles as well as the Uniform System of Accounts prescribed by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). Accordingly, they do not include all the information and footnotes required for the annual report. In the opinion of management, all adjustments (consisting of normal and recurring accruals) considered necessary for a fair presentation have been included. Operating results for the three-month period ended March&#160;31,&#160;2026 are not necessarily indicative of the results that may be expected and ultimately realized for the year ending December 31, 2026. The interim financial statements should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and accompanying notes of Colonial Pipeline ("Colonial" or "the Company") presented in the 2025 Form 6 Annual Report.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Legal Contingencies and Environmental Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Matters Pertaining to Customer Actions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On February 1, 2024, one of Colonial's shippers filed a new complaint with the FERC asserting that the Company's indexed rates are unjust and unreasonable and further challenging the Company's market-based rates. Five additional shippers subsequently filed similar complaints. On April 2, 2025, the FERC issued an order consolidating the six complaints that were outstanding as of that date into one proceeding (Docket No. OR24-3). With that order, the FERC also dismissed the challenges to Colonial's market-based rates and referred the challenges to the indexed rates to a hearing process, suspending that hearing process pending a FERC settlement process. On May 23, 2025, a seventh shipper filed a complaint (Docket No. OR25-8). On September 24, 2025, this shipper's complaint was consolidated into the same proceeding as the previously filed six complaints. On May 4, 2026, an order was issued terminating the settlement procedures and designating a presiding administrative law judge. The FERC assigned the complaint to a Track 3 schedule, reserved for complex cases. The order established that the hearing must be convened within 42 weeks, and the initial decision must be issued within 63 weeks. As of the date of this report, Colonial has settled with certain shippers. Colonial has substantial defenses to these complaints and will vigorously assert these defenses. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;FERC Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The FERC indexing system provides for annual index rate adjustments effective no earlier than July 1st of each year. The indexing system currently applies to a majority of the Company&#8217;s published tariff rates. Colonial elected to adjust its index rates in each of the periods presented within this report in keeping with the FERC indexing system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On November 20, 2025, the FERC issued a Notice of Proposed Rulemaking (NOPR) to seek comment on a proposed index level used to determine annual changes to oil pipeline rate ceilings for the five-year period commencing on July 1, 2026. The FERC proposed to use the Producer Price Index for Finished Goods (PPI-FG) minus 1.42% as the index level for the five-year period. Comments to this NOPR were submitted. On April 24, 2026, the FERC issued a final rule establishing a new oil pipeline index level of PPI-FG minus 0.55% for the five-year period commencing July 1, 2026. This rule is subject to appeal.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Subsequent Events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Colonial has evaluated events subsequent to the balance sheet date but prior to June&#160;9, 2026, the date the financial statements were available for issuance, that would have a material impact on these Form 6-Q financial statements. Any material subsequent events that occurred during this time have been properly disclosed in the accompanying notes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
